1
00:02:49,750 --> 00:02:51,030
Burn them all!

2
00:02:51,810 --> 00:02:53,120
Where's my sister?

3
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,590
Burn them all!

4
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:26,750
Please.

5
00:03:41,920 --> 00:03:43,730
Burn them. Burn them all!

6
00:03:57,840 --> 00:03:59,210
Burn them all!

7
00:04:08,710 --> 00:04:09,650
Meera.

8
00:04:12,040 --> 00:04:13,170
They found us.

9
00:04:21,030 --> 00:04:22,260
I'm so sorry.

10
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:29,470
Come with me, now.

11
00:05:34,650 --> 00:05:36,000
The dead don't rest.

12
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:03,800
It's so green.

13
00:06:04,350 --> 00:06:05,360
Oh, yes.

14
00:06:06,110 --> 00:06:07,650
Once you get south of the Riverlands,

15
00:06:07,650 --> 00:06:10,160
very different sorts of trees start to take over.

16
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:14,590
Maple, elm, beech, poplar.

17
00:06:18,410 --> 00:06:19,580
The odd willow.

18
00:06:20,760 --> 00:06:22,850
And of course now that summer's over,

19
00:06:22,850 --> 00:06:25,280
you'll start seeing the autumn colors coming in.

20
00:06:28,120 --> 00:06:31,990
Still, you'll find more green here than anywhere else.

21
00:06:31,990 --> 00:06:35,580
You're nervous. You're a nervous talker.

22
00:06:40,720 --> 00:06:43,380
That's not any better being a nervous mute.

23
00:06:43,870 --> 00:06:45,420
I didn't think I'd ever come back here

24
00:06:45,430 --> 00:06:49,110
after my father made me renounce my title and inheritance

25
00:06:50,020 --> 00:06:51,920
and, well, threaten to kill me if I didn't.

26
00:06:53,970 --> 00:06:56,570
A person just doesn't feel welcome at that point.

27
00:06:58,440 --> 00:07:01,410
And I certainly didn't expect to be introducing him to my family.

28
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:05,520
So you know what to tell them.

29
00:07:06,150 --> 00:07:07,440
That Little Sam is your baby.

30
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:09,320
Yes, now that's very important.

31
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:11,610
If he thinks that Little Sam is his grandchild,

32
00:07:11,610 --> 00:07:12,820
he'll take you in.

33
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,240
He'll get an education. He'll learn to read.

34
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:20,520
And you can help teach him. Huh?

35
00:07:21,070 --> 00:07:23,160
What did you tell your family about me?

36
00:07:27,090 --> 00:07:29,470
I told them I met you in the North.

37
00:07:29,470 --> 00:07:31,360
Did you tell them how far north?

38
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:34,320
Well, it wasn't a very large piece of parchment.

39
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:36,350
You didn't tell them where I'm really from?

40
00:07:36,350 --> 00:07:38,070
You didn't tell them I'm a wildling?

41
00:07:38,070 --> 00:07:39,220
The thing is...

42
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:42,410
my father doesn't like wildlings.

43
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:45,220
He hoped I'd make a man of myself by

44
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:47,150
"Killing some bloody wildlings,"

45
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:50,760
so it's probably a good subject to avoid if at all possible.

46
00:07:54,670 --> 00:07:55,880
I think we're here.

47
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:26,600
Sam.

48
00:08:27,290 --> 00:08:29,280
Oh, Sam.

49
00:08:29,290 --> 00:08:30,720
Oh, hello, Mother.

50
00:08:34,610 --> 00:08:36,120
I never thought I'd see you again.

51
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,850
You look wonderful.

52
00:08:42,130 --> 00:08:43,140
Talla?

53
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:45,810
Gods, you're a woman now.

54
00:08:45,810 --> 00:08:48,330
Father says I have to marry Symun Fossoway.

55
00:08:48,680 --> 00:08:51,520
- He has yellow teeth-- - That's enough, Talla.

56
00:08:53,810 --> 00:08:57,910
Oh, um, Mother, this is Gilly.

57
00:09:00,190 --> 00:09:01,370
Oh, my.

58
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:04,470
You are lovely.

59
00:09:06,810 --> 00:09:09,490
I am happy to know you, Lady Tarly.

60
00:09:12,730 --> 00:09:15,060
Oh, and this,

61
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:18,200
this is our son Samwell.

62
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:24,780
Hello, little one.

63
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:29,070
It's me, your grandmother.

64
00:09:31,010 --> 00:09:32,160
May I hold him?

65
00:09:33,250 --> 00:09:34,850
Yes, of course.

66
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:43,010
You have a curious mind, I can tell.

67
00:09:43,650 --> 00:09:46,690
You'll be a scholar like your father.

68
00:09:47,350 --> 00:09:50,500
Where is Father? And Dickon?

69
00:09:51,070 --> 00:09:52,620
They're on a hunt.

70
00:09:53,550 --> 00:09:54,980
They'll join us for dinner.

71
00:09:55,890 --> 00:09:59,160
Come inside. Such a journey.

72
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:00,810
You must be exhausted.

73
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:04,620
Come, you'll be wanting a bath after all that travel.

74
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:06,500
Oh, and a dress for dinner.

75
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:08,020
You can wear one of mine.

76
00:10:08,430 --> 00:10:09,790
What's your color?

77
00:10:10,270 --> 00:10:12,810
Midnight blue or silver?

78
00:10:12,810 --> 00:10:15,150
Silver, maybe. Come.

79
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:17,720
You can choose one of my bedrooms if you want.

80
00:10:26,700 --> 00:10:28,080
Is there no other way?

81
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:30,510
You're afraid for her?

82
00:10:31,410 --> 00:10:33,150
Of course I'm afraid for her!

83
00:10:36,370 --> 00:10:39,630
It just seems very dangerous.

84
00:10:39,630 --> 00:10:41,970
She'll be protected the entire way.

85
00:10:42,780 --> 00:10:44,820
The Faith Militant are very stern

86
00:10:44,820 --> 00:10:47,270
with those who overstep their bounds.

87
00:10:49,450 --> 00:10:53,080
And Queen Margaery isn't your mother.

88
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:55,980
I suspect the gods will predispose the common people

89
00:10:55,980 --> 00:10:58,190
to gentleness on her behalf.

90
00:10:58,400 --> 00:11:00,860
She's truly opened her heart to them.

91
00:11:01,650 --> 00:11:05,180
She's always been very devoted to the poor and the unfortunate.

92
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:07,960
And now she's devoted to the gods as well.

93
00:11:10,640 --> 00:11:12,100
Would you like to see her?

94
00:11:34,450 --> 00:11:35,600
Have they hurt you?

95
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:37,300
Have they mistreated you?

96
00:11:37,330 --> 00:11:40,150
- No, Your Grace. - I've missed you.

97
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:42,270
More than you could know.

98
00:11:42,460 --> 00:11:44,410
We'll be together again soon

99
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:47,260
and everything will be better than it was before.

100
00:11:47,750 --> 00:11:48,830
Better how?

101
00:11:49,330 --> 00:11:50,470
Soon the--

102
00:11:53,450 --> 00:11:54,760
walk of atonement.

103
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:57,860
He says there's no other way.

104
00:11:59,270 --> 00:12:01,790
Have you spoken to him at all, the High Sparrow?

105
00:12:02,100 --> 00:12:04,680
Yes, a few times.

106
00:12:05,910 --> 00:12:07,030
Have you?

107
00:12:07,030 --> 00:12:08,200
Yes, I have.

108
00:12:08,580 --> 00:12:10,820
He's not quite what we thought he was, is he?

109
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:15,230
You think I'm mad.

110
00:12:15,230 --> 00:12:16,450
I sound mad.

111
00:12:17,930 --> 00:12:19,550
No. No, you don't.

112
00:12:19,550 --> 00:12:21,640
You-- you could never.

113
00:12:21,730 --> 00:12:23,380
You're right, he's not.

114
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:24,920
He's a lot more--

115
00:12:25,210 --> 00:12:26,270
He is.

116
00:12:27,210 --> 00:12:28,750
There's something about him.

117
00:12:29,090 --> 00:12:30,980
His way of looking at the world.

118
00:12:33,890 --> 00:12:38,000
It's not an easy thing admitting to yourself what you really are.

119
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:40,470
It's taken me a while.

120
00:12:41,150 --> 00:12:42,430
He's helped me.

121
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:45,210
What are you talking about?

122
00:12:45,350 --> 00:12:49,540
You're a good person. You've always been a good person.

123
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:52,360
You're the best person I know.

124
00:12:53,010 --> 00:12:55,460
I was just telling him about your devotion to the poor.

125
00:12:55,460 --> 00:12:57,620
Ah, yes, I visited their hovels

126
00:12:57,620 --> 00:13:01,160
and I fed them soup and I made sure I was seen doing it.

127
00:13:02,900 --> 00:13:05,380
I never gave them what they really needed, though.

128
00:13:06,490 --> 00:13:10,930
I've had lots of time to think about how good I was at seeming good.

129
00:13:12,410 --> 00:13:14,900
All those stories I told myself about who I was

130
00:13:14,900 --> 00:13:17,510
and why I did the things I did.

131
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:21,900
There were so many lies in those stories.

132
00:13:23,540 --> 00:13:24,890
I don't understand.

133
00:13:24,890 --> 00:13:27,070
It's all right. It really is.

134
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:30,970
It's such a relief to let go of those lies.

135
00:13:36,070 --> 00:13:37,480
What about Loras?

136
00:13:40,210 --> 00:13:41,670
I love my brother.

137
00:13:42,030 --> 00:13:43,910
I will always love my brother.

138
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:49,720
His soul is pure and perfect.

139
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:52,260
His sins don't erase that purity,

140
00:13:52,260 --> 00:13:54,140
they only obscure it.

141
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:59,050
He just needs to atone for them.

142
00:14:00,290 --> 00:14:01,580
We all do.

143
00:14:02,050 --> 00:14:04,540
Sooner or later, one way or another.

144
00:14:06,140 --> 00:14:09,010
The gods have a plan for us all.

145
00:14:24,900 --> 00:14:26,910
It's hard to walk in this.

146
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:31,020
It's beautiful.

147
00:14:33,650 --> 00:14:35,090
You're beautiful.

148
00:15:22,790 --> 00:15:25,980
This venison, it's very tasty.

149
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:28,290
Is it from today's hunt?

150
00:15:29,330 --> 00:15:30,790
Well, no.

151
00:15:30,790 --> 00:15:32,490
We haven't been able to cure that one yet.

152
00:15:33,090 --> 00:15:34,430
This is last week's.

153
00:15:35,660 --> 00:15:37,640
Oh, of course. Sorry.

154
00:15:38,710 --> 00:15:39,900
Long journey.

155
00:15:41,210 --> 00:15:43,030
Brought it down from 70 yards.

156
00:15:43,030 --> 00:15:44,180
One shot.

157
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:48,250
Oh, that's a fair distance.

158
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,530
So do you do much hunting up at the Wall?

159
00:15:51,910 --> 00:15:53,620
Oh, yes. Yes.

160
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:55,950
A good amount.

161
00:15:56,980 --> 00:15:58,450
North of the Wall,

162
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:00,620
you don't hunt, you don't eat.

163
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:04,340
Mostly deer or is it elk as well?

164
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,160
Rabbits.

165
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:10,260
Sometimes squirrels.

166
00:16:13,490 --> 00:16:17,300
I say "We," It's my friend Jon mostly.

167
00:16:17,860 --> 00:16:19,360
Sometimes Edd.

168
00:16:20,010 --> 00:16:21,260
Oh, and Gilly.

169
00:16:21,270 --> 00:16:24,210
She's-- she's quite a good hunter as well.

170
00:16:24,810 --> 00:16:26,590
Um, huntress.

171
00:16:27,900 --> 00:16:29,700
I imagine it's common where you're from.

172
00:16:30,070 --> 00:16:31,220
We once met a man,

173
00:16:31,220 --> 00:16:33,650
Lord Umber from Last Hearth, wasn't it, Randyll,

174
00:16:33,810 --> 00:16:36,040
who said he taught all his daughters how to hunt.

175
00:16:36,210 --> 00:16:38,150
Your father taught you to hunt?

176
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:40,820
Our father would never teach us.

177
00:16:40,870 --> 00:16:44,140
I think our father could learn a thing or two from your father.

178
00:16:44,510 --> 00:16:45,830
That's enough of that.

179
00:16:49,090 --> 00:16:50,970
Samwell, would you care for more bread?

180
00:16:52,190 --> 00:16:53,780
Yes. Yes, please.

181
00:16:53,780 --> 00:16:54,920
Thank you, Mother.

182
00:16:59,810 --> 00:17:01,390
Not fat enough already?

183
00:17:13,760 --> 00:17:16,510
I travelled south under orders from the Lord Commander.

184
00:17:16,850 --> 00:17:18,590
- He wants me to-- - I read your letter.

185
00:17:20,790 --> 00:17:22,980
You're to be a maester.

186
00:17:23,430 --> 00:17:26,130
Yes. And once I have my chain,

187
00:17:26,130 --> 00:17:28,590
I'll return to Castle Black.

188
00:17:28,780 --> 00:17:31,600
I thought the Night's Watch might make a man of you.

189
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:35,580
Something resembling a man at least.

190
00:17:36,950 --> 00:17:40,600
You managed to stay soft and fat.

191
00:17:42,540 --> 00:17:45,210
Your nose buried in books.

192
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:49,560
Spending your life reading about the achievements of better men.

193
00:17:50,070 --> 00:17:53,410
I'll wager you still can't sit a horse or wield a sword.

194
00:17:53,410 --> 00:17:56,450
Randyll, to be maester of the Night's Watch is a great honor.

195
00:17:56,450 --> 00:17:58,270
He can wield a sword.

196
00:18:00,670 --> 00:18:02,270
He killed a Thenn.

197
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:05,880
He killed a white walker.

198
00:18:08,220 --> 00:18:09,510
There's no such thing.

199
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:14,590
I saw it with my own eyes on our way down to Castle Black.

200
00:18:15,050 --> 00:18:17,820
He drove a dagger into the walker's heart.

201
00:18:18,080 --> 00:18:21,370
He risked his own life to save mine more than once.

202
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:24,510
He's a greater warrior than either of you will ever be.

203
00:18:27,890 --> 00:18:30,330
Your way down to Castle Black?

204
00:18:33,630 --> 00:18:35,710
Where did he kill a white walker?

205
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:39,960
Where are you from?

206
00:18:40,450 --> 00:18:42,180
How'd you come to meet my son?

207
00:18:45,370 --> 00:18:47,600
The Night's Watch came to our keep.

208
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:49,330
- Where? - Gilly.

209
00:18:49,330 --> 00:18:51,590
- North of the Wall. - North of the Wall?

210
00:18:56,230 --> 00:18:57,920
You're a wildling.

211
00:19:05,850 --> 00:19:07,450
The Seven Kingdoms have waged war

212
00:19:07,450 --> 00:19:09,510
against these savages for centuries

213
00:19:09,510 --> 00:19:12,920
and here I sit hosting one in my hall

214
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,320
thanks to my son.

215
00:19:19,010 --> 00:19:20,380
See that sword?

216
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:24,570
It's called Heartsbane.

217
00:19:26,390 --> 00:19:29,170
It's been in our family for 500 years.

218
00:19:29,670 --> 00:19:31,570
It's Valyrian steel.

219
00:19:32,190 --> 00:19:34,620
Only a handful of them left in the world.

220
00:19:35,030 --> 00:19:38,080
It's supposed to go to my firstborn son after I die.

221
00:19:39,060 --> 00:19:40,210
To him.

222
00:19:41,390 --> 00:19:44,760
He will never wield that sword.

223
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:48,910
If he were to become Lord Tarly of Horn Hill,

224
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:51,110
it would be the end of this house.

225
00:19:54,540 --> 00:19:57,030
I took you for a Mole's Town whore when I saw you

226
00:19:57,030 --> 00:19:58,830
and I made my peace with that.

227
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:00,420
Who else would have him?

228
00:20:02,590 --> 00:20:04,430
But I overestimated him.

229
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:06,980
No.

230
00:20:09,610 --> 00:20:13,500
It was a wildling whore that seduced my son.

231
00:20:15,650 --> 00:20:17,590
This you getting back at me, boy?

232
00:20:21,050 --> 00:20:23,870
Bringing that to my table and making me dine with it?

233
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:28,890
And you got what you were after, didn't you?

234
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:33,110
A bastard. A half-breed bastard.

235
00:20:33,750 --> 00:20:36,510
Your invitation into our home.

236
00:20:36,990 --> 00:20:39,150
Come, my dear. Talla.

237
00:20:40,380 --> 00:20:41,920
I've lost my appetite.

238
00:20:42,760 --> 00:20:44,290
He dishonors us.

239
00:20:44,290 --> 00:20:45,970
You dishonor yourself.

240
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:54,390
Your mother's a fine woman. You're not worthy of her.

241
00:20:57,450 --> 00:20:59,070
To please her, I'll take the wildling in.

242
00:20:59,070 --> 00:21:00,670
She can work in the kitchens.

243
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:04,350
The bastard will be raised here.

244
00:21:07,420 --> 00:21:10,730
But this will be the last night you ever spend at Horn Hill.

245
00:21:18,740 --> 00:21:20,580
I'm sorry I let him treat you that way.

246
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:24,600
I was afraid he'd turn you and Little Sam away.

247
00:21:25,900 --> 00:21:27,590
I'm not angry at you.

248
00:21:28,570 --> 00:21:30,470
I'm angry that horrible people

249
00:21:30,470 --> 00:21:33,120
can treat good people that way and get away with it.

250
00:21:38,820 --> 00:21:40,210
When do you have to go?

251
00:21:43,440 --> 00:21:44,650
First light.

252
00:21:56,170 --> 00:21:57,900
Say good-bye to him for me.

253
00:22:06,290 --> 00:22:08,560
You're not what he thinks you are, Sam.

254
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:11,280
He doesn't know what you are.

255
00:22:15,290 --> 00:22:16,580
Good-bye, Gilly.

256
00:23:01,960 --> 00:23:03,320
- Sam? - We're leaving.

257
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:05,650
- What? - Get your things.

258
00:23:06,200 --> 00:23:08,070
I don't have any things.

259
00:23:08,470 --> 00:23:10,920
- What are you doing? - We belong together.

260
00:23:11,490 --> 00:23:12,660
All of us.

261
00:23:14,500 --> 00:23:15,970
What about your mother and sister?

262
00:23:15,970 --> 00:23:17,510
Oh, they'll understand.

263
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:19,710
Your sister's dress.

264
00:23:19,710 --> 00:23:21,190
She won't mind.

265
00:23:23,790 --> 00:23:25,570
Looks better on you anyway.

266
00:23:26,610 --> 00:23:28,060
Sam.

267
00:23:28,160 --> 00:23:29,960
That's your father's sword.

268
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:32,140
It's my family's sword.

269
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:38,350
Sam.

270
00:23:38,410 --> 00:23:40,040
Won't he come for it?

271
00:23:42,590 --> 00:23:44,280
He can bloody well try.

272
00:23:49,340 --> 00:23:51,300
The lion and the rose are one.

273
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:53,580
I thank the gods above.

274
00:23:53,580 --> 00:23:55,970
And to you, my beauteous bride,

275
00:23:55,970 --> 00:23:58,510
I pledge undying love.

276
00:23:58,750 --> 00:24:02,860
Hail King Joffrey. Hail Queen Margaery.

277
00:24:02,900 --> 00:24:05,280
I'll drink a toast to my new queen,

278
00:24:05,280 --> 00:24:07,430
for there is no one fairer.

279
00:24:07,970 --> 00:24:09,910
Dear Uncle, will you share my joy

280
00:24:09,910 --> 00:24:12,240
and be my royal cupbearer?

281
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:14,860
Drink long and deep, my noble king,

282
00:24:14,860 --> 00:24:16,950
from this cup of sweet wine.

283
00:24:17,530 --> 00:24:19,890
The last drink he shall ever take.

284
00:24:19,900 --> 00:24:22,390
And vengeance shall be mine.

285
00:24:34,060 --> 00:24:35,270
Poison!

286
00:24:36,010 --> 00:24:37,310
Murder!

287
00:24:37,310 --> 00:24:40,410
I gasp. I-- I die.

288
00:24:42,280 --> 00:24:43,470
I limp.

289
00:24:45,490 --> 00:24:47,670
And it was he...

290
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:50,580
that poisoned me.

291
00:24:50,750 --> 00:24:53,390
My evil Uncle Imp.

292
00:25:05,860 --> 00:25:07,370
My firstborn son.

293
00:25:08,110 --> 00:25:09,930
My golden lion

294
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:12,850
foully, falsely slain.

295
00:25:14,490 --> 00:25:17,010
I pray you found a lasting peace

296
00:25:17,400 --> 00:25:19,710
free from strife and pain.

297
00:25:21,840 --> 00:25:23,970
Hear my prayer, Oh cruel gods.

298
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:25,830
Take my life instead.

299
00:25:26,220 --> 00:25:29,640
For I cannot face another day when my sweet boy is dead.

300
00:25:30,290 --> 00:25:31,500
Oh, woe.

301
00:25:33,090 --> 00:25:34,770
Oh, grief.

302
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:39,910
Oh, darkest day, my heart is full of sorrow.

303
00:25:42,740 --> 00:25:44,400
All hope is lost.

304
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:48,020
All joy is gone.

305
00:25:51,310 --> 00:25:53,250
And there is no tomorrow.

306
00:26:13,950 --> 00:26:16,690
What is that I hear and smell?

307
00:26:16,690 --> 00:26:19,570
Someone I'll soon send to hell.

308
00:26:19,570 --> 00:26:22,500
It's time to see if truth they told

309
00:26:22,500 --> 00:26:26,070
who said Tywin Lannister shits gold.

310
00:26:28,030 --> 00:26:30,160
You beast. You beast.

311
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:34,970
You killed my wife and now you've taken your father's life.

312
00:26:35,010 --> 00:26:38,110
No worse child ever stained this land.

313
00:26:38,110 --> 00:26:40,250
Curse the day I named you.

314
00:26:49,860 --> 00:26:53,800
My greatest crime. Now I must flee.

315
00:26:53,800 --> 00:26:56,390
Then sail across the Narrow Sea

316
00:26:56,390 --> 00:27:00,370
to do unto you more treachery.

317
00:27:00,660 --> 00:27:04,850
Don't fear winter. Fear me!

318
00:27:08,700 --> 00:27:10,030
Thank you.

319
00:27:10,580 --> 00:27:14,030
Ladies and gentlemen, I give you Bianca,

320
00:27:14,390 --> 00:27:15,910
Clarenzo.

321
00:27:15,910 --> 00:27:18,610
I give you Bobono.

322
00:27:19,790 --> 00:27:22,150
I give you Camello.

323
00:27:23,230 --> 00:27:24,770
And last but not least,

324
00:27:24,770 --> 00:27:26,940
sweet Lady Crane.

325
00:27:38,560 --> 00:27:41,950
Give this a good beating. Shake those fleas out. That's a dear.

326
00:27:42,230 --> 00:27:44,170
That crowd was shit.

327
00:27:48,650 --> 00:27:49,810
Girl.

328
00:27:50,670 --> 00:27:52,290
What are you doing back here?

329
00:27:53,650 --> 00:27:54,800
Nothing.

330
00:27:54,820 --> 00:27:57,930
I saw you the other day in the audience.

331
00:27:57,930 --> 00:28:00,600
How many times have you seen this stupid play?

332
00:28:02,910 --> 00:28:04,190
Three times.

333
00:28:04,190 --> 00:28:05,460
Did you pay?

334
00:28:06,690 --> 00:28:07,850
No.

335
00:28:11,690 --> 00:28:14,020
I remember when the players came to my village.

336
00:28:14,020 --> 00:28:16,170
I didn't have any money, so I snuck in.

337
00:28:16,350 --> 00:28:17,780
Just like you.

338
00:28:18,770 --> 00:28:20,980
Saw the painted faces, the costumes,

339
00:28:20,980 --> 00:28:22,700
listened to the songs,

340
00:28:22,750 --> 00:28:26,170
cried when the young lovers died in each other's arms.

341
00:28:27,070 --> 00:28:28,810
I ran off and joined them the next day,

342
00:28:28,810 --> 00:28:30,010
never looked back.

343
00:28:31,460 --> 00:28:32,910
You're very good.

344
00:28:32,910 --> 00:28:35,280
My final speech is shit.

345
00:28:35,290 --> 00:28:38,000
But to be fair to myself, which I always like to be,

346
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:39,590
the writing's no good.

347
00:28:40,590 --> 00:28:42,010
So change it.

348
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:45,350
It would all just be farting, belching,

349
00:28:45,350 --> 00:28:46,970
and slapping without you.

350
00:28:48,440 --> 00:28:50,160
How would you change it?

351
00:28:56,040 --> 00:28:58,850
The queen loves her son more than anything.

352
00:28:59,830 --> 00:29:02,410
And he was taken from her before she could say good-bye.

353
00:29:02,410 --> 00:29:04,370
She wouldn't just cry.

354
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:09,860
She would be angry.

355
00:29:11,210 --> 00:29:13,640
She would want to kill the person who did this to her.

356
00:29:17,800 --> 00:29:19,290
What's your name?

357
00:29:20,870 --> 00:29:22,280
Mercy.

358
00:29:23,420 --> 00:29:26,090
You have very expressive eyes, Mercy.

359
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:28,640
Wonderful eyebrows.

360
00:29:29,260 --> 00:29:31,380
Do you like pretending to be other people?

361
00:29:33,170 --> 00:29:35,930
I have to go. My father's waiting for me.

362
00:29:44,130 --> 00:29:46,590
Lady Crane, they loved you.

363
00:29:47,080 --> 00:29:49,750
They were sweet. Or drunk.

364
00:29:50,450 --> 00:29:52,040
Drunkenly sweet.

365
00:29:52,050 --> 00:29:53,980
No laugh for Ned's death.

366
00:29:54,280 --> 00:29:57,390
These people are worse than animals.

367
00:29:58,590 --> 00:30:01,530
But they loved her. They all love her.

368
00:30:01,970 --> 00:30:05,190
Yes, you are adored by people and animals alike.

369
00:30:05,190 --> 00:30:07,250
I do what I can with what I'm given.

370
00:30:08,220 --> 00:30:09,650
With what you're given?

371
00:30:10,070 --> 00:30:11,790
Well, I was thinking--

372
00:30:11,790 --> 00:30:13,730
Oh, we're all thinkers now, are we?

373
00:30:13,730 --> 00:30:16,200
Full to the tits with ideas.

374
00:30:16,930 --> 00:30:19,780
- I didn't mean-- - You have ideas, I have ideas,

375
00:30:19,780 --> 00:30:21,500
he has ideas.

376
00:30:21,640 --> 00:30:24,550
Why should my ideas have any more value than yours

377
00:30:24,550 --> 00:30:27,060
simply because I've been doing this my whole life?

378
00:30:28,020 --> 00:30:30,140
Who is anyone to judge my work?

379
00:30:30,140 --> 00:30:32,440
This is my profession. I know what I'm doing.

380
00:30:33,430 --> 00:30:35,420
You have no right to an opinion.

381
00:30:48,430 --> 00:30:50,060
Careful of that one.

382
00:30:54,760 --> 00:30:56,420
She wants you dead.

383
00:31:35,890 --> 00:31:37,250
And?

384
00:31:37,460 --> 00:31:39,200
As I expected.

385
00:31:41,320 --> 00:31:42,650
A shame.

386
00:31:43,090 --> 00:31:45,180
A girl had many gifts.

387
00:31:48,520 --> 00:31:50,060
You promised me.

388
00:31:56,210 --> 00:31:57,860
Don't let her suffer.

389
00:32:49,890 --> 00:32:52,780
Company, halt!

390
00:32:54,280 --> 00:32:55,490
My lord.

391
00:32:56,030 --> 00:32:57,170
My lord.

392
00:32:58,700 --> 00:33:02,930
My friends, the hour has come.

393
00:33:03,440 --> 00:33:06,790
Madness has overtaken this city

394
00:33:06,790 --> 00:33:11,350
and grasped in its claws my children.

395
00:33:11,830 --> 00:33:14,820
But now we must drive it back

396
00:33:14,820 --> 00:33:17,860
under the rocks whence it came.

397
00:33:18,210 --> 00:33:22,440
Madness has had its day!

398
00:33:25,770 --> 00:33:28,260
Forward, march!

399
00:33:30,030 --> 00:33:33,840
Rich or poor, noble or common,

400
00:33:34,950 --> 00:33:38,530
if we sin, we must atone.

401
00:33:39,860 --> 00:33:42,830
Margaery of House Tyrell

402
00:33:43,010 --> 00:33:45,330
came to us a sinner.

403
00:33:45,980 --> 00:33:47,600
She stood before the gods

404
00:33:47,600 --> 00:33:50,170
in the holy sept and lied.

405
00:33:50,480 --> 00:33:53,280
She turned a blind eye to her brother's sins.

406
00:33:53,290 --> 00:33:55,570
She disgraced her house,

407
00:33:56,200 --> 00:33:59,660
her king, and herself.

408
00:34:31,380 --> 00:34:33,300
Company, halt!

409
00:34:33,300 --> 00:34:35,120
Face front!

410
00:34:35,540 --> 00:34:36,830
Turn!

411
00:34:39,050 --> 00:34:40,420
Lord Tyrell.

412
00:34:42,480 --> 00:34:43,680
Ser Jaime.

413
00:34:44,780 --> 00:34:46,270
Sorry to interrupt.

414
00:34:46,270 --> 00:34:49,200
We're here for Queen Margaery and Ser Loras Tyrell.

415
00:34:49,260 --> 00:34:51,870
Give them to us and we'll be on our way.

416
00:34:53,190 --> 00:34:56,080
I don't have the authority to give them to you.

417
00:34:56,670 --> 00:34:59,350
And you don't have the authority to take them.

418
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:01,110
That's right.

419
00:35:03,990 --> 00:35:05,110
Hyah.

420
00:35:10,320 --> 00:35:11,950
Lock spears!

421
00:35:13,950 --> 00:35:17,610
I speak for King Tommen of House Baratheon, First of His Name.

422
00:35:17,720 --> 00:35:21,050
The gods don't recognize his authority in this matter.

423
00:35:21,090 --> 00:35:23,700
You've already insulted one great house.

424
00:35:23,920 --> 00:35:25,720
It won't happen twice.

425
00:35:25,720 --> 00:35:27,830
Every last sparrow will die

426
00:35:27,830 --> 00:35:30,650
before Margaery Tyrell walks down that street.

427
00:35:31,150 --> 00:35:32,940
To die in the service of the gods

428
00:35:32,950 --> 00:35:35,270
would please each and every one of us.

429
00:35:35,450 --> 00:35:37,110
We yearn for it.

430
00:35:46,940 --> 00:35:49,080
But there is no call for it today.

431
00:35:51,910 --> 00:35:55,130
There will be no walk of atonement.

432
00:36:12,140 --> 00:36:13,560
Order up.

433
00:36:13,560 --> 00:36:16,880
Queen Margaery has already atoned for her sins

434
00:36:17,510 --> 00:36:19,320
by bringing another

435
00:36:19,490 --> 00:36:22,150
into the true light of the Seven.

436
00:36:51,840 --> 00:36:54,470
Together we announce

437
00:36:55,290 --> 00:36:57,620
a new age of harmony.

438
00:36:58,390 --> 00:37:00,170
A holy alliance

439
00:37:00,580 --> 00:37:03,940
between the Crown and the Faith.

440
00:37:20,600 --> 00:37:23,520
Long live King Tommen and bless you, Queen Margaery!

441
00:37:23,530 --> 00:37:26,040
The Crown and the Faith

442
00:37:26,380 --> 00:37:29,690
are the twin pillars upon which the world rests.

443
00:37:30,110 --> 00:37:35,050
Together we will restore the Seven Kingdoms to glory.

444
00:37:53,900 --> 00:37:55,500
What's happening?

445
00:37:56,030 --> 00:37:57,540
He's beaten us.

446
00:37:57,730 --> 00:37:59,350
That's what's happening.

447
00:38:14,740 --> 00:38:18,010
When you attack the Faith, you attack the Crown.

448
00:38:18,230 --> 00:38:20,720
Anyone who attacks the Crown is unfit

449
00:38:20,730 --> 00:38:23,210
to serve as Lord Commander of the Kingsguard.

450
00:38:23,580 --> 00:38:27,190
I've been a member of the Kingsguard since before you were born.

451
00:38:29,170 --> 00:38:32,170
You don't have to do this. You don't have to do anything.

452
00:38:34,890 --> 00:38:36,720
I have to answer to the gods.

453
00:38:36,730 --> 00:38:39,110
Not when you're sitting in that chair.

454
00:38:43,150 --> 00:38:45,810
The Crown's decision on this matter is final.

455
00:38:47,760 --> 00:38:50,240
Will I be walking naked in the streets?

456
00:38:50,450 --> 00:38:53,370
Or will I spend a few months in the Sept dungeons first

457
00:38:53,370 --> 00:38:55,620
to teach me about the gods' mercy?

458
00:38:59,890 --> 00:39:01,560
You have served your house

459
00:39:01,560 --> 00:39:03,690
and your king faithfully for many years.

460
00:39:04,340 --> 00:39:05,950
And you will continue to do so.

461
00:39:08,240 --> 00:39:09,870
But not in this city.

462
00:39:13,200 --> 00:39:16,460
You've lost it?

463
00:39:18,680 --> 00:39:19,630
Yes, Father.

464
00:39:19,630 --> 00:39:22,590
It's a castle, not a bloody sheep.

465
00:39:22,980 --> 00:39:25,420
Presumably you still know where it is.

466
00:39:26,010 --> 00:39:28,090
You didn't lose Riverrun.

467
00:39:28,160 --> 00:39:30,380
You let the Blackfish take it from you.

468
00:39:30,380 --> 00:39:33,310
He surprised us. He knows the castle better than anyone.

469
00:39:33,320 --> 00:39:36,810
You did lose the Blackfish after the Red Wedding.

470
00:39:36,810 --> 00:39:39,910
You had him right here in this hall and you let him leave.

471
00:39:39,910 --> 00:39:42,090
Then when I told you to hunt him down and kill him,

472
00:39:42,090 --> 00:39:43,370
you couldn't find him.

473
00:39:43,950 --> 00:39:46,160
That's what it means to lose something.

474
00:39:46,160 --> 00:39:48,870
Now he's come back and taken Riverrun.

475
00:39:50,290 --> 00:39:51,870
I don't think it's fair to blame us--

476
00:39:51,870 --> 00:39:55,080
For 300 years we kissed Tully boots,

477
00:39:55,090 --> 00:39:59,020
swore oaths to them and their stinking fish banners.

478
00:39:59,020 --> 00:40:01,450
Not again. Riverrun is ours.

479
00:40:01,580 --> 00:40:02,950
Take it back.

480
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:05,190
We don't have the men.

481
00:40:05,190 --> 00:40:08,830
We've got 10 times as many men as the damn Blackfish.

482
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:12,260
The Mallisters have risen against us. And the Blackwoods.

483
00:40:12,260 --> 00:40:15,310
The Brotherhood Without banners is rallying the commoners against us,

484
00:40:15,310 --> 00:40:17,370
raiding our supply trains and camps.

485
00:40:17,370 --> 00:40:20,350
Riverrun can withstand a siege for a year.

486
00:40:21,240 --> 00:40:24,090
If I want excuses, I'll put her in charge.

487
00:40:24,090 --> 00:40:25,830
They're laughing at us.

488
00:40:25,870 --> 00:40:27,900
All across the Riverlands

489
00:40:27,900 --> 00:40:29,600
right down to King's Landing,

490
00:40:29,600 --> 00:40:31,590
they're laughing at us.

491
00:40:31,830 --> 00:40:33,900
I hear it in my sleep!

492
00:40:34,230 --> 00:40:37,670
I'm not dead yet, unfortunately for you.

493
00:40:37,670 --> 00:40:39,200
And I'll not leave this world

494
00:40:39,200 --> 00:40:42,010
until they all choke on that laughter.

495
00:40:42,240 --> 00:40:44,220
Take that castle back.

496
00:40:45,920 --> 00:40:48,150
He'll never yield, Father.

497
00:40:48,550 --> 00:40:50,960
Oh, he'll yield.

498
00:40:55,630 --> 00:40:57,710
You'll show him the knife

499
00:40:57,790 --> 00:41:02,060
you used to kill Robb Stark's child in his whore mother's belly,

500
00:41:02,330 --> 00:41:04,060
and you'll show him the knife

501
00:41:04,060 --> 00:41:06,690
you used to open his niece's throat.

502
00:41:06,690 --> 00:41:08,270
And you'll remind him

503
00:41:08,270 --> 00:41:12,400
who it was that got married at the Red Wedding in the first place.

504
00:41:13,180 --> 00:41:14,330
His nephew.

505
00:41:30,160 --> 00:41:32,100
Cheer up, Lord Edmure.

506
00:41:32,960 --> 00:41:34,380
You're going home.

507
00:41:35,250 --> 00:41:38,130
I'm being sent to deal with the Blackfish.

508
00:41:38,670 --> 00:41:41,130
Apparently Walder Frey can't manage it on his own

509
00:41:41,130 --> 00:41:43,230
because he's 400 years old.

510
00:41:43,490 --> 00:41:45,640
Sent me with an army to the Riverlands

511
00:41:45,640 --> 00:41:47,620
and a siege that could last months.

512
00:41:47,620 --> 00:41:50,290
Better you're elsewhere at the head of an army

513
00:41:50,290 --> 00:41:52,050
than in the sept dungeons.

514
00:41:53,150 --> 00:41:54,900
I'm not going to the Riverlands.

515
00:41:58,130 --> 00:41:59,060
What, then?

516
00:41:59,700 --> 00:42:03,280
I'm going to give Bronn the largest bag of gold anyone's ever seen

517
00:42:03,670 --> 00:42:06,100
and have him gather the best killers he knows.

518
00:42:06,690 --> 00:42:07,920
I'll take them to the sept

519
00:42:07,920 --> 00:42:09,750
and I'll remove the High Sparrow's head

520
00:42:09,750 --> 00:42:11,920
and every other sparrow head I can find.

521
00:42:11,930 --> 00:42:12,670
You can't.

522
00:42:12,680 --> 00:42:15,040
He has our son! He stole our son!

523
00:42:15,890 --> 00:42:17,470
He's torn our family apart.

524
00:42:17,470 --> 00:42:20,180
How should we treat people who tear us apart?

525
00:42:21,230 --> 00:42:23,550
We should treat them without mercy and we will.

526
00:42:24,690 --> 00:42:27,000
But if you kill the High Sparrow, you won't leave the sept alive.

527
00:42:27,000 --> 00:42:28,890
And without you, this is all for nothing.

528
00:42:30,570 --> 00:42:33,090
Stand at the head of our army where you belong,

529
00:42:33,770 --> 00:42:35,140
where Father wanted you.

530
00:42:36,220 --> 00:42:38,600
Show our men where their loyalties belong.

531
00:42:38,600 --> 00:42:40,610
Show them what Lannisters are,

532
00:42:40,610 --> 00:42:42,710
what we do to our enemies.

533
00:42:44,110 --> 00:42:46,290
And take that stupid little castle back

534
00:42:46,290 --> 00:42:48,730
because it's ours and because you can.

535
00:42:48,740 --> 00:42:51,930
You'll stand trial soon. I need to be here for you.

536
00:42:53,060 --> 00:42:55,070
It will be a trial by combat.

537
00:42:56,530 --> 00:42:57,980
I have the Mountain.

538
00:43:00,710 --> 00:43:03,390
They've made us both stronger, all of them.

539
00:43:05,010 --> 00:43:07,020
They have no idea how strong we are.

540
00:43:07,570 --> 00:43:09,610
No idea what we're going to do to them.

541
00:43:20,210 --> 00:43:21,880
We've always been together.

542
00:43:22,630 --> 00:43:24,510
We'll always be together.

543
00:43:25,170 --> 00:43:27,300
We're the only two people in the world.

544
00:43:47,780 --> 00:43:49,180
Why did you help us?

545
00:43:52,680 --> 00:43:54,250
The Three-Eyed Raven sent for me.

546
00:43:54,250 --> 00:43:55,670
The Three-Eyed Raven's dead.

547
00:43:56,530 --> 00:43:57,750
Now he lives again.

548
00:44:10,610 --> 00:44:12,960
When I last saw you, you were a boy.

549
00:44:14,440 --> 00:44:15,590
A fearless boy.

550
00:44:16,230 --> 00:44:19,910
Loved to climb the castle walls, frighten his mother.

551
00:44:20,770 --> 00:44:21,680
Who are you?

552
00:44:39,980 --> 00:44:41,220
Uncle Benjen.

553
00:44:42,960 --> 00:44:44,130
The last letter Jon wrote me

554
00:44:44,140 --> 00:44:45,870
said you had been lost beyond the Wall.

555
00:44:49,320 --> 00:44:51,700
I led a ranging party deep into the North

556
00:44:51,700 --> 00:44:53,200
to find white walkers.

557
00:44:54,630 --> 00:44:55,680
They found us.

558
00:44:56,580 --> 00:44:59,990
A white walker stabbed me in the gut with a sword of ice.

559
00:45:02,760 --> 00:45:03,920
Left me there to die.

560
00:45:04,480 --> 00:45:05,350
To turn.

561
00:45:06,900 --> 00:45:08,190
The Children found me.

562
00:45:09,130 --> 00:45:11,660
Stopped the walker's magic from taking hold.

563
00:45:11,770 --> 00:45:12,550
How?

564
00:45:12,670 --> 00:45:15,420
The same way they made the walkers in the first place.

565
00:45:15,420 --> 00:45:16,790
You saw it yourself.

566
00:45:18,480 --> 00:45:19,760
Dragonglass.

567
00:45:21,660 --> 00:45:24,210
A shard of dragonglass plunged into your heart.

568
00:45:26,270 --> 00:45:28,240
You are the Three-Eyed Raven now.

569
00:45:29,400 --> 00:45:32,200
I didn't have time to learn. I can't control anything.

570
00:45:34,880 --> 00:45:36,490
You must learn to control it

571
00:45:37,240 --> 00:45:38,980
before the Night King comes.

572
00:45:41,510 --> 00:45:42,340
Drink.

573
00:45:45,620 --> 00:45:48,460
One way or another,

574
00:45:48,760 --> 00:45:51,080
he will find his way to the world of men.

575
00:45:52,200 --> 00:45:53,130
When he does,

576
00:45:53,900 --> 00:45:56,040
you will be there waiting for him.

577
00:45:57,520 --> 00:45:58,880
And you will be ready.

578
00:46:21,110 --> 00:46:22,080
Everything all right?

579
00:46:23,280 --> 00:46:24,930
How many days' ride to Meereen?

580
00:46:25,580 --> 00:46:26,740
A week at best.

581
00:46:27,610 --> 00:46:30,500
How many ships will I need to bring my khalasar to Westeros?

582
00:46:31,000 --> 00:46:33,000
Dothraki and all their horses,

583
00:46:33,010 --> 00:46:34,980
the Unsullied, the Second Sons--

584
00:46:35,650 --> 00:46:37,700
1,000 ships easily.

585
00:46:37,700 --> 00:46:39,900
- Probably more. - And who has that many?

586
00:46:40,260 --> 00:46:41,050
Nobody.

587
00:46:42,130 --> 00:46:43,280
Nobody yet.

588
00:46:45,440 --> 00:46:46,720
So we ride for Meereen

589
00:46:46,720 --> 00:46:48,940
and after that we sail for Westeros.

590
00:46:49,160 --> 00:46:50,090
And what then?

591
00:46:50,950 --> 00:46:52,380
I take what is mine.

592
00:46:53,680 --> 00:46:56,750
You weren't made to sit on a chair in a palace.

593
00:46:56,880 --> 00:46:58,330
What was I made for?

594
00:46:59,940 --> 00:47:02,580
You're a conqueror, Daenerys Stormborn.

595
00:47:11,440 --> 00:47:12,320
Wait here.

